diff --git a/docs/INSTALL.md b/docs/INSTALL.md
index 4611920..63424b5 100644
--- a/docs/INSTALL.md
+++ b/docs/INSTALL.md
@@ -159,6 +159,19 @@ gets 1.25 × DPI. Without it, windows get 230 per unit of scale.
 
 The density persists. Desktop tiling determines the window's available size.
 
+### Window controls
+
+Droidloom prefers compositor-provided title bars. On GNOME Wayland, or when a
+compositor requests client-side decorations instead, it draws its own title bar
+with close, minimize and maximize/restore buttons. Drag the title bar to move a
+window, or drag its borders to resize it. Fullscreen windows hide the title bar.
+This does not change GNOME's settings or require a desktop extension.
+
+The title bar is outside Android's content area, so it does not consume Android
+touch coordinates or change app DPI. Standard desktop shortcuts still work:
+on GNOME, **Alt+F4** closes, **Super+H** minimizes and **Alt+Space** opens the
+window menu.
+
 ## 5. Install an APK
 
 The installation command accepts a **single, standalone APK**. Native x86_64
